Cyde Weys <vze23tnc@verizon.net> writes:
> Also, can someone tell me what this one means?
> 
> M1_THICK_HIDE	Has a thick hide or scales (ex: crocodile)
> 
> What effect does it have in the game?  Does a monster being thick scaled 
> have some sort of effect on resistance rolls?  I'm writing a 
> spoiler/article on this and help would be appreciated.  Thanks.

>From include/mondata.h:

  #define thick_skinned(ptr)      (((ptr)->mflags1 & M1_THICK_HIDE) != 0L)

thick_skinned is checked in various parts of the combat code: to
reduce kick damage taken to 0, to prevent you dealing the monster a
staggering barehanded strike, to reduce a bullwhip's physical damage
to 0, and to separate ghosts and shades from xorns and earth
elementals to get the pick-axe to-hit bonus right.

